   "subject": "plotting linear vs non linear effects",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">Hello,</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">I thought that this would be an easy task but I am really struggling with this.</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">I am trying to compare visually the effect of x assuming a linear vs non linear relationship with y</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35);min-height:15px\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"></span><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">formula= y ~ x + spatial and temporal effects  # for linear effect</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">formula= y ~  f(inla.group(x), model=&quot;rw2&quot;) + spatial and temporal effects   #for non linear effect</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35);min-height:15px\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"></span><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">Here is the model:</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">mod=inla(formula, data=Data, family=&#39;nbinomial, control.compute=list(E=weights)</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35);min-height:15px\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"></span><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">I can plot the mean +/- 1 SD </span> non linear effect <span style=\"letter-spacing:0px\"> as:</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35);min-height:15px\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"></span><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">plot(mod$summary.random[[1]][,1], mod$summary.random[[1]][,2])</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35);min-height:15px\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"></span><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">lines(mod$summary.random[[1]][,1], (mod$summary.random[[1]][,2]-mod$summary.random[[1]][,3]))</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35);min-height:15px\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"></span><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">lines(mod$summary.random[[1]][,1], (mod$summary.random[[1]][,2]+mod$summary.random[[1]][,3]))</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35);min-height:15px\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"></span><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">and for plotting the linear effect, I would need to subtract the mean of x (I guess) as:</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35);min-height:15px\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"></span><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">plot (Data$x, mod$summary.fixed[[2,1]]*Data$x-mean(mod$summary.fixed[[2,1]]*Data$x))</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35);min-height:15px\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"></span><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">However I don’t know how to create SD intervals here that are analogous to the ones created for the non-linear response. </span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">Any help would be deeply appreciated.</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35);min-height:15px\"><br><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\"></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;line-height:normal;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(35,35,35)\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.0px\">Victor.</span></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
