   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; and for plotting the linear effect, I would need to subtract the mean\r<br>&gt; of x (I guess) as:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; plot (Data$x, mod$summary.fixed[[2,1]]*Data$x-mean(mod\r<br>&gt; $summary.fixed[[2,1]]*Data$x))\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; However I don’t know how to create SD intervals here that are\r<br>&gt; analogous to the ones created for the non-linear response. \r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "I see; this does not follow from the output directly. you have the\r<br>uncertainly for beta.x, in \r<br>\t\r<br>\t.... + beta.x * x + ...\r<br>\r<br>isn&#39;t that enough?  do you want to look at beta.x*x  as a regressoon\r<br>curve and compute the uncertainty for the regression curve itself? can\r<br>you do this using &#39;linear combinations&#39; f.ex ??\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>-- \r<br>Håvard Rue\r<br>Department of Mathematical Sciences\r<br>Norwegian University of Science and Technology\r<br>N-7491 Trondheim, Norway\r<br>Voice:  <a href=\"tel:+47%2073%2059%2035%2033\" value=\"+4773593533\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+47-7359-3533</a>    URL  : <a href=\"http://www.math.ntnu.no/~hrue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.math.ntnu.no/~hrue&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792445796732000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jbl5gDM5YUOvodl8PwnzT\">http://www.math.ntnu.no/~hrue</a>  \r<br>Mobile: <a href=\"tel:+47%2092%2060%2000%2021\" value=\"+4792600021\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+47-9260-0021</a>    Email: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">havar...@math.ntnu.no</a>\r<br>\r<br>R-INLA: <a href=\"http://www.r-inla.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.r-inla.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792445796733000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2-lYTHf6UTTChLWMbhARj-\">www.r-inla.org</a>\r<br>\r<br>"
